"""MSA module for AlphaFold3 -- fused CUDA implementation.

4-block MSA module: each block runs MSA row attention -> OPM -> PairBlock.

The eager reference is ~590 tiny kernel launches for the captured 16-residue /
8-sequence shape and is entirely launch-bound (2.3 ms of GPU work inside 7.8 ms
of wall clock).  This implementation keeps the reference module tree (so weights
load by name) and replaces the forward with 25 hand-written CUDA kernels whose
CTA->data ownership is aligned across phase boundaries, so a launch is spent
only where the dataflow is genuinely all-to-all.

Reference: openfold3/core/model/latent/msa_module.py MSAModuleStack
"""

